      prompt: '<b>2-bromo-2-methylbutane</b> <mol smiles="CCC(C)(C)Br" label="2-bromo-2-methylbutane"></mol> is heated with KOH in ethanol. HO⁻ is a strong base, and an alkene with more carbon groups on its C=C is more stable (lower in energy). Which alkene is the major product? (Ignore E/Z.)',
